<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
    The Stars half of the pair at the top of Home.

    One ground, `surface_card`, shared with every other card on the screen;
    the ACCENT LIVES IN THE BORDER. That is the rule the whole home screen now
    follows, and it replaced a tinted-ground scheme that had each card sitting
    on its own coloured wash. Two reasons it had to go:

      * a 16% gold tint over a warm ground mixes to olive, so the surfaces
        meant to read as premium read as disabled instead, and
      * four differently-tinted grounds in one scroll left no neutral for the
        eye to rest on, which is what made the screen feel assembled.

    A shared ground plus a coloured hairline says the same thing more quietly:
    these are the same kind of object, and this one is about Stars.
-->
<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:shape="rectangle">
    <solid android:color="@color/surface_card" />
    <stroke android:width="1dp" android:color="@color/stars_stroke" />
    <corners android:radius="18dp" />
</shape>
